# Acceptance expectations for ONE cohort you hold locally. Copy this file to
# expected.local.tsv and fill each value from that cohort's own recorded tables.
# expected.local.tsv is gitignored: these numbers describe data the reader does not have.
#
# Tier 1 is deterministic, so every value here must reproduce EXACTLY and nothing in it
# carries a tolerance. A BLANK value is a FAILURE, not a skip - a checkpoint with nothing
# to compare against can never fail.
#
# The checkpoint names below are exactly the ones run_tier1.py checks, and it checks no
# others. If you override `fail_columns` in schema.local.tsv, replace the four `only_*`
# rows: each is named only_<column name with its fail_ prefix removed>.
tier	checkpoint	value
